From 0f304451b8cf65098ba1eccdd920d4da108777d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LightCraft additional extensions <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:26:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] One-click Lightroom Classic keyboard shortcut set

Help > Keyboard Shortcuts (and Settings > General > Keyboard) gain
"Shortcut set: Lightroom (default) | Lightroom Classic"; app.keyProfile
{profile: "lightroom"|"classic"} switches it from the control channel.
The choice is saved as settings.keyProfile in ui.json (read leniently:
older or unknown values are Lightroom). The user's own keymap entries
still win over either set.

Classic gives the commands Lightroom Classic's keys where LightCraft has
them (E Loupe, D Develop, C Compare, R Crop, Q Remove, K Brush, M / Shift+M
gradients, Shift+W Masking, L Lights Out, I info overlay, H tool overlay,
Shift+T Guided Upright, Cmd+U Auto, Cmd+Shift+S Sync, Cmd+N version /
album by context, Cmd+Shift+E Export, Cmd+E other editor, Cmd+Alt+E
PhotoCraft, Shift+P pick and advance, Ctrl+Y redo) and moves every key
that would clash. Adapted from upstream PR #2338, ported to v0.20.0 and
the module bar commands. Mapping in docs/classic-keymap.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
